WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.507
A physical dosage form releases medicine over time. A

00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:08.239
mathematical model tries to describe that changing

00:00:08.239 --> 00:00:08.837
process.

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:17.730
Formulation composition, geometry and transport

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:21.334
assumptions affect simulated release. The selected

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:24.506
equations embody choices that need scrutiny.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.617
The book chapter examines simulation of drug release

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:34.823
and

00:00:34.823 --> 00:00:38.192
performance prediction using virtual models within

00:00:38.192 --> 00:00:40.011
pharmaceutical development.

00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:49.372
Without calibration and suitable validation, a model

00:00:49.372 --> 00:00:49.576
can

00:00:49.576 --> 00:00:52.429
produce elegant curves and still make poor

00:00:52.429 --> 00:00:53.244
predictions.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:01.684
Mechanistic assumptions, parameter uncertainty and

00:01:01.684 --> 00:01:05.031
extrapolation beyond known experiments all limit

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.589
credible

00:01:05.589 --> 00:01:07.644
digital performance forecasts.

00:01:13.758 --> 00:01:17.582
A defensible virtual model can guide test design, but

00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:17.798
the

00:01:17.798 --> 00:01:20.136
laboratory decides what survives.
